# kube-network-policies (ADR 0086), the NetworkPolicy enforcer: a static binary built from source at
# the commit that tag v1.1.3 of the public repository is. The commit, not the tag, is the pin:
# build.sh fetches that object and fails unless HEAD is it, and a tag can be moved.
#
# Why this release (chosen 2026-11-23, from the repository's tags and its GitHub releases): v1.1.3
# is the newest stable release, published more than two weeks before that date.
#
# Moved by: the PM, in a pull request that reruns `make image` and `make image-repro` and the QEMU
# test that starts a Kubernetes cluster, when a later release is at least two weeks old or an
# advisory is published for the pinned one. No bot proposes it.
KNP_REPO=https://github.com/kubernetes-sigs/kube-network-policies
KNP_VERSION=v1.1.3
KNP_COMMIT=d3fc697c1acaa0c8872c262ff3e04d8299eac6b3
# Licences (SPDX), read from the COPYING or LICENSE of each source and checked by naru-release (ADR 0076).
KNP_LICENSE=Apache-2.0
